filex-office-editor (scripts/x2t), BRF Tech, 2026-10-16: the SVG engine's
copy of the CSS calculator gets a namespace of its own in a WebAssembly
build.

ONLYOFFICE core builds its CSS calculator (Common/3dParty/html/css) twice:
into graphics, for the SVG engine (css_calculator_without_xhtml), and into
HtmlFile2, with CSS_CALCULATOR_WITH_XHTML - which adds members to
NSCSS::CNode, NSCSS::CStyleStorage and NSCSS::CCssCalculator_Private.
Natively the two are separate libraries and each keeps its own copy. In one
WebAssembly module they met: CryptPad's recipe left graphics' copy out (the
two clashed at the link), so the SVG engine, compiled for the smaller
layout, ran HtmlFile2's code for the larger one; and the std::vector code
both instantiate for NSCSS::CNode (push_back, its relocation, its
destruction) was kept once, graphics', with the smaller element size, for
HtmlFile2 too.

Measured (2026-10-16, emscripten 4.0.11, wasm32): NSCSS::CNode is 60 bytes
here and 64 in HtmlFile2, CStyleStorage 60 and 72, CCssCalculator_Private 76
and 100 - so every metafile x2t opened (MetaFile::CMetaFile holds an SVG
file, whose calculator is allocated with 76 bytes and initialised with 100)
wrote past its block. A build with function names showed where it ended:
  - a PDF of a document with SVG pictures (the DS's sample.docx):
    SVG::CSvgCalculator::SetData, std::vector<NSCSS::CNode>'s destruction,
    free() aborting on the broken heap;
  - a .doc with EMF/WMF pictures into the editor's format (picture.doc) and
    sample.xlsx into a PDF: CSvgFile::Clear, CStyleStorage::Clear,
    ~CElement, "memory access out of bounds";
  - HTML to md, of any HTML (<p>Hello</p> too): HTML::CHTMLReader::
    GetSubClass, std::vector<NSCSS::CNode>::push_back moving 64-byte nodes
    with graphics' 60-byte code, a segmentation fault (SAFE_HEAP) - or a
    loop, depending on what the bytes held.
With graphics' sources built again in a namespace of their own
(steps.sh no longer drops them), each library has its copy, as natively.

git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line on.

diff --git a/DesktopEditor/graphics/pro/metafile.pri b/DesktopEditor/graphics/pro/metafile.pri
index bc3b103a..5c5f1962 100644
--- a/DesktopEditor/graphics/pro/metafile.pri
+++ b/DesktopEditor/graphics/pro/metafile.pri
@@ -184,6 +184,18 @@ METAFILE_PATH = $$PWD/../../raster/Metafile
 
 		CONFIG += css_calculator_without_xhtml
 
+		# filex-office-editor (BRF Tech, 2026-10-16): in a WebAssembly build
+		# every library is linked into one module, HtmlFile2 with them, and
+		# HtmlFile2 builds the same CSS calculator with
+		# CSS_CALCULATOR_WITH_XHTML, which lays NSCSS::CNode,
+		# NSCSS::CStyleStorage and NSCSS::CCssCalculator_Private out
+		# differently (wasm32: 64, 72 and 100 bytes; 60, 60 and 76 here).
+		# Natively each library keeps its own copy (hidden symbols); in one
+		# module the two would meet - the same functions defined twice, the
+		# same std::vector<NSCSS::CNode> code instantiated by both and kept
+		# once. This copy gets a namespace of its own instead.
+		core_wasm:DEFINES += NSCSS=NSCSS_Svg
+
 		include($$METAFILE_PATH/../../../Common/3dParty/html/css/CssCalculator.pri)
 	}
 }
